{"text": "Because Missus Mallard was afflicted with heart trouble, great care was taken to break the news of her husbands death to her as gently as possible. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> It was her sister Josephine who told her, in broken sentences and veiled hints that revealed the truth while half hiding it. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Her husbands friend Richards was there too, because he had been in the newspaper office when news of the railroad disaster arrived. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Brently Mallards name had led the list of the killed, and Richards, who wanted to be sure, had checked it with a second telegram. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> He had then hurried to the Mallards house, hoping to arrive before any less careful and less tender friend could bring the sad message. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> She did not hear the story as many women have heard the same, with a frozen inability to accept what it meant. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> She wept at once, with sudden, wild abandonment, in her sisters arms, and her whole body shook with the force of her tears. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> When the storm of grief had spent itself, she went away to her room alone, and she would have no one follow her.", "alignment": {"characters": ["B", "e", "c", "a", "u", "s", "e", " ", "M", "i", "s", "s", "u", "s", " ", "M", "a", "l", "l", "a", "r", "d", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "a", "f", "f", "l", "i", "c", "t", "e", "d", " ", "w", "i", "t", "h", " ", "h", "e", "a", "r", "t", " ", "t", "r", "o", "u", "b", "l", "e", ",", " ", "g", "r", "e", "a", "t", " ", "c", "a", "r", "e", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "t", "a", "k", "e", "n", " ", "t", "o", " ", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "n", "e", "w", "s", " ", "o", "f", " ", "h", "e", "r", " ", "h", "u", "s", "b", "a", "n", "d", "s", " ", "d", "e", "a", "t", "h", " ", "t", "o", " ", "h", "e", "r", " ", "a", "s", " ", "g", "e", "n", "t", "l", "y", " ", "a", "s", " ", "p", "o", "s", "s", "i", "b", "l", "e", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " 